<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US midterm elections: 'Maybe the best colour for Texas is purple'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f7a4e6c59df91a7ccfc6bfc481eb9f96b3705a08269ff94bac600f1690f9183</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-maybe-the-best-colour-for-texas-is-purple" /><summary type="html">Texas flipped blue following the US midterm elections, marking a historic shift for a state that hasn't been led by Democrats in decades. The legacy of prolonged Republican leadership has left a lasting mark, but as Democrat James Talarico said with this election, 'maybe the best colour for Texas is purple.' FRANCE 24's Texas correspondent Andres Espinal reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Is Republican Party able to pivot away from MAGA movement, or will it sputter forward leaderless?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:166a443e5bbe6f354acf0d2491715cefc72ced0e320e9a5b800784437e70d6f0</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:16:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/is-republican-party-able-to-pivot-away-from-maga-movement-or-will-it-sputter-forward-leaderless" /><summary type="html">Does an electoral repudiation of Donald Trump also mark the beginning of MAGA’s decline? Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Ian Reifowitz, SUNY Distinguished Professor of Historical Studies at Empire State University, who describes the Republican defeat as “an absolute and complete repudiation” of the president. He connects voters’ economic frustrations with resentment over presidential enrichment, while questioning whether ideological differences between progressive and moderate Democrats proved decisive. Looking towards 2028, Reifowitz identifies a central Republican dilemma: “If JD Vance is the nominee, he can’t run against Donald Trump”, yet Trump himself may refuse to relinquish control of the party.</summary></entry><entry><title>French blood banks foil new cyberattack targeting refrigerators</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c081e9236900e92a7713b1b6e2a3fdfed8b5fdd35c029a55d664efd8c96a83a9</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:10:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261104-french-blood-banks-foil-new-cyberattack-targeting-refrigerators" /><summary type="html">A cyberattack in France targeted three cold stores containing donated blood samples and plasma, authorities said on Wednesday. The incident – which was unsuccessful due to the facilities' alarm systems – is the latest in a series of suspected attacks that have targeted refrigerators in European supermarkets, as well as French cooperative bank, Credit Mutuel Arkea, which was also affected Wednesday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Gen Z gives Democrats their strongest support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce37c4959dabfb711407b4f084848cc1a17aae8a23b6368b890a6cc805bd69b5</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterm-elections-gen-z-gives-democrats-their-strongest-support" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, 50 million members of Gen Z were eligible to vote. Young voters gave Democrats the strongest support, with 75% of them voting for the party. This generation will be the biggest voting bloc in the United States in the coming years. FRANCE 24's Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>How Trump's broken promises on war, inflation handed Democrats the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08d5aeeeb3efe517536aac85c48ec1f1a071b42ded44922b0b5493d39039f280</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:02:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-how-trump-s-broken-promises-on-war-inflation-handed-democrats-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Speaking to Fox News following the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump admitted that inflation was likely one reason Republicans did poorly. Many Americans have been frustrated with how the Iran war has pushed up prices, including at the gasoline pump, especially given that Trump had campaigned for his second term on a pledge of “no new wars”, as Ellen Gainsford explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: How Abdul El-Sayed used 'humour and hope' to rebuff racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d1ba87b9cf829198ab08e85eb1de99f31d8aecb900a7e1a1b73823661191bdd</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:25:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-how-abdul-el-sayed-used-humour-and-hope-to-rebuff-racism" /><summary type="html">Abdul El-Sayed is set to become the first Muslim senator in US history following his midterms victory in Michigan. His victory came despite what he has denounced as racist attacks against him, inlcuding from Donald Trump, which, says FRANCE 24's correspondent Jessica Le Masurier, he rebuffed with a mixture of "humour and hope".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks to shift blame but has 'nowhere to hide' after midterms defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e893829383849cd56c44132fa208d21eac46ce1e215ea9ae9242cfc067364dfb</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:13:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-seeks-to-shift-blame-but-has-nowhere-to-hide-after-midterms-defeat" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has sought to shift the blame for the Republicans' defeat at the midterms by claiming that if he had been on the ballot the party would have won. But the "blue wave" that saw Democrats win control of Congress can be traced directly back to Trump's decisions, says France 24's Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: 'It is now going to be pretty chaotic for Donald Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fc8ca0798b20da646ef433b97225e3c36a662c5aed828d3acde44c700d68c4d</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:12:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-it-is-now-going-to-be-pretty-chaotic-for-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">The Democrats' victory in the midterm elections have left Donald Trump in a difficult position for the rest of his mandate. The now "blue" House of Representatives will decide the budget, which Trump will have to accept and follow. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian's 'not expecting drastic change in US policy' after midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8666e39596255dfc418ce90a65affbfaf2e79c857cfe0040e5e8a028f840a300</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:26:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-s-not-expecting-drastic-change-in-us-policy-after-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukrainians do not expect the Democrats' victory in the US midterm elections is change much in regards to US policy on the war with Russia, or at least not quickly, says France 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky has not reacted yet to the "blue wave" taking control of Congress in the US.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look back at how Trump's political decisions saw his approval rating plummet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f248966570e28492ef9f8cf26212a10fa0adcbcfd3db17d2b4013824479cbe9</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:17:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-a-look-back-at-how-trump-s-political-decisions-saw-his-approval-rating-plummet" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's unpopularity has been cited as a major factor in the Democrats' sweeping victory in the midterms. The latest polls show Trump's approval rating has plummeted to 37.3%, down from 42% in his first midterm election. What were the political decisions that led to such a dramatic decline?</summary></entry><entry><title>Blue wave sweeps across America: 'In 1974, we had Watergate babies, now we have Iran War babies'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ffe152c97b0a508a1b8abe7c1cbd441d34b934ac076726ae132acb8e2476d4c</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:00:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/blue-wave-sweeps-across-america-in-1974-we-had-watergate-babies-now-we-have-iran-war-babies" /><summary type="html">Stuart Norval welcomes France 24 International Affairs Editor Philip Turle and Hind Ziane, Geopolitical analyst and founder / CEO of Genpo. "In 1974, we had the Watergate babies. Now we have the Iran War babies," remarks Ziane with this striking historical analogy. Just as the Watergate scandal helped propel a new generation of Democratic lawmakers into Congress in 1974, Zian argues that public disillusionment with the Iran war, mounting economic pressures and dissatisfaction with Donald Trump's leadership may now be reshaping the American political landscape. Yet Turle reminds us, "They're not voting for Democrats because they love the Democrats. They're voting for the Democrats because they don't like Donald Trump."</summary></entry><entry><title>'Like a cancer': How data centres became a key issue at midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a506f45522095714489bac42ab84430ea673c01d8833d7dbe4fe65215d73f8d</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:54:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-like-a-cancer-how-data-centres-became-a-key-issue-at-midterms" /><summary type="html">Over 5,000 data centres are now scattered across the US, some near ubran centes, generating noise pollution and consuming large amount of electricity. Donald Trump has long defended the construction of these mega structures, which are essential for big tech companies to run. But voters, including many Republicans, say they are feeling betrayed by their government.</summary></entry><entry><title>What consequences for Israel as Democrats win the US midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c123168b53215e159f59fdd59183a8c5a3d27f343beb88a86f20abc2440101e9</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:32:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Democrats seized control of the US Congress on Tuesday, capturing the Senate and House of Representatives in a stunning upset. What are the potential consequences for Israel and Benjamin Netanyahu, as Trump announced on Tuesday that the US will halt $3.8 billion in aid to the country? FRANCE 24's correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump reacts to the Democrats’ sweeping victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c058a23355636db13358dae3306e7de6acaf9ca258a074d4e1fb535f3e0f8ae2</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:24:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-trump-reacts-to-the-democrats-sweeping-victory" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump had rare praise for rival Democrats Tuesday after their stunning US midterm elections victory and admitted the Iran war may have played a part in the defeat of his Republican Party. But the 80-year-old refused to take any personal responsibility for the result.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia expands hydropower ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:332f7626c64dbaf45a23b541c84ba0927f91207583976183a3aeb99880f5b19f</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:19:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-ethiopia-expands-hydropower-ambitions" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia is looking to position itself as an African leader in clean energy, as it prepares to host next year’s COP32 climate summit. Alongside the GERD, the country is building another massive hydropower project on the Omo River in the southwest, as it expands electricity production and exports power to neighbouring countries. This report from our correspondent Tom Canetti.</summary></entry><entry><title>From Kansas to Texas, Democrats win big in Republican heartlands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53ca92adbb5b98d180a228c50499e68ef546461d00f8b695fcff09345bcd1e79</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:15:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-from-kansas-to-texas-democrats-win-big-in-republican-heartlands" /><summary type="html">The Democrats are set to take control of both the House and the Senate following victories in states like South Carolina, Kansas, and Texas, whose switching blue constitutes an historic upset. President Donald Trump has said he will accept the results and blames the candidates themselves for the losses.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms bring surge of historic firsts for women and minorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d4446045836afd0cbf27e4b03091448c5b0c4ab91f9638a3e37fab1fd17f796</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:15:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-us-midterms-bring-surge-of-historic-firsts-women-members-minority-groups" /><summary type="html">The 2026 US midterm elections will go down in history for the Democrats' dramatic takeover of both houses of Congress but also for a surge of historic firsts for women, LGBT, Black and Native American candidates, as well as the election of the first Muslim US senator.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea pushes digital detox for young people addicted to screens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1684ee6f730b76a3b572c0885c1191b4d1e805136713421ab0a7152a76fa657</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:14:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261104-south-korea-pushes-digital-detox-for-young-people-addicted-to-screens" /><summary type="html">Back in August, France's Constitutional Council overturned a social media ban for children under 15. Some students, though, are now banned from using their smartphones at school. In South Korea, where an estimated 40 percent of young children and teens are addicted to their mobile devices, authorities are trying to find ways to drastically reduce their screen time – a huge challenge in such a hyper-connected society. FRANCE 24's Chloé Borgnon, Aruna Popuri and Justin McCurry report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Midterms: Trump acknowledges role of Iran war, congratulates Dems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b64f4426f70710e75238e2b3fe04cb8634aaba34c92b3cc7a0c61082205f88a</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:13:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-trump-acknowledges-role-of-iran-war-congratulates-dems" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump acknowledged on Wednesday that the US-Israeli war on ​Iran ‌played a role in his party's sweeping ⁠defeat in the midterm elections, as Democrats won control of the House of ‌Representatives and the Senate. "I think a part of it ⁠was Iran," Trump told Fox News in an interview in which he also praised the Democrats for their campaign. France 24's Wassim Cornet has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US voters back abortion rights and reject Trump's gerrymandering in state ballot measures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5a948f442c69ce21de145c1db133c6142f679ff4a7cdbf3be82a6b8e00f8efe</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:49:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-us-voters-back-abortion-rights-and-reject-trump-s-gerrymandering-in-state-ballot-measures" /><summary type="html">US voters in several states pushed back on President Donald Trump’s redistricting efforts and backed abortion rights in 145 ballot questions during the midterm elections. Some measures put Trump’s priorities to a public test by gauging support for his attempts to redraw congressional districts, limit reproductive rights and strengthen voter identification requirements.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Markets react with caution to Democrats' victory in US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53f89903116c7b9ba3deaf6f61dc7b6412d8c72247e4bca5373bf909506edc0b</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:40:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261104-markets-react-with-caution-to-democrats-victory-in-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">Investors shunned AI stocks and turned to government bonds on Wednesday in the wake of the Democratic Party's takeover of Congress in the US midterm elections. Oil prices meanwhile ticked slightly higher, as uncertainty remains over the direction of US President Donald Trump's war against Iran. Also in this edition, we focus on the central issue of this midterm campaign: the rise in the cost of living.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Champions League: Paris Saint-Germain make easy work of Villarreal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a31c64dfa92a60e195e53eb4b0b1dcf7bdc1717bd679b5507f97b262ceaf0d30</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261104-champions-league-paris-saint-germain-make-easy-work-of-villarreal" /><summary type="html">Paris Saint-Germain made easy work of Villarreal in the Champions League (6-0). The game was decided after 17 minutes and four goals.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo residents sue Chinese mining giant for widespread pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d04d03e172abf92277adac643c6b0465b54af2730ed357c3044607f303c577bf</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:22:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-dr-congo-residents-sue-chinese-mining-giant-for-widespread-pollution" /><summary type="html">In Kolwezi, the mining capital of the Democratic Republic of Congo, local residents are suing a huge Chinese mine and the government for environmental pollution. It will be one of the most important cases the country has seen. FRANCE 24's correspondent Emmet Livingstone reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>30 million South Africans registered to vote across nine provinces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fab6d83c3f8887226fd14babd9dd8c49d402504afce74bbc6bfcc53e3d37d39</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-30-million-south-africans-registered-to-vote-across-nine-provinces" /><summary type="html">In South Africa, around 30 million people have registered to cast their votes across the country's nine provinces. The economy is at the forefront of the November 4 local elections. The spotlight is on Gauteng, a province long plagued by governance challenges. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.</summary></entry></feed>
